      "rev_n_2_610a45_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_610a45_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_610a45",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Instead of using dynamic programming to track the maximum and minimum values directly, use a greedy approach to select segments that maximize the difference between the maximum and minimum values in the resulting array. Focus on segments that cover large ranges and have significant impact on reducing the minimum value while increasing the maximum value. This approach simplifies the problem and avoids the complexities associated with dynamic programming in this context.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_610a45_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_7fcaef4ebf",
        "created_at": 1794499775.7131257
      },
      "rev_n_1_0e6e04_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_0e6e04_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_0e6e04",
        "thought_text": "Evaluate all possible subsets of segments and calculate the resulting array \\( b \\) for each subset, but ensure that the segments are applied in a way that maximizes the difference between the maximum and minimum values in the resulting array \\( b \\). This involves checking each combination of segments and computing the difference after applying them, keeping track of the combination that yields the highest difference.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_0e6e04_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_332203eb4d",
        "created_at": 1794499810.187288
      },
      "rev_n_3_d30a2c_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_d30a2c_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_d30a2c",
        "thought_text": "Consider sorting the segments based on their impact on the array's range, but prioritize segments that cover larger portions of the array to ensure a more significant change in the range. Additionally, use a greedy approach to select segments that maximize the range without overlapping excessively, ensuring that each segment contributes optimally to the final array.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_d30a2c_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_d4d7e1f613",
        "created_at": 1794499845.4403138
      },
